","n_etimologia":1,"categoria":"prestito","incerta":"no","significato":"slingshot","termine_origine":"рога́тка","catena":[{"codice":"ru","nome":"Russian","termine":"рога́тка","categoria":"prestito"}],"lontana":"ru","ambiti":[],"via":"","testo":"From Russian рога́тка f (rogátka, “slingshot; fourhorn sculpin”)."},{"parola":"שוקולד","pos":"noun","n_etimologia":1,"categoria":"prestito","incerta":"no","significato":"chocolate (a food made from ground roasted cocoa beans)","termine_origine":"шокола́д","catena":[{"codice":"ru","nome":"Russian","termine":"шокола́д","categoria":"prestito"}],"lontana":"ru","ambiti":[],"via":"","testo":"Borrowed from Russian шокола́д (šokolád)."},{"parola":"שחמט","pos":"noun","n_etimologia":1,"categoria":"prestito","incerta":"sì","motivo_incerta":"Probably","significato":"chess (a board game for two players, each beginning with sixteen chess pieces moving according to fixed rules across a…","termine_origine":"ша́хматы","catena":[{"codice":"ru","nome":"Russian","termine":"ша́хматы","categoria":"prestito"},{"codice":"fa","nome":"Persian","termine":"شاه مات","categoria":"non_precisato"},{"codice":"de","nome":"German","termine":"Schachmatt","categoria":"non_precisato"}],"lontana":"de","ambiti":[],"via":"","testo":"Probably from Russian ша́хматы (šáxmaty, “chess”), from Persian شاه مات (šâh mât, “checkmate”). The final stress may be due to the predominant Hebrew accent and/or influenced by German Schachmatt (“checkmate”)."},{"parola":"תיקן","pos":"noun","n_etimologia":2,"categoria":"non_precisato","incerta":"sì","motivo_incerta":"perhaps","significato":"cockroach","termine_origine":"тарака́н","catena":[{"codice":"ru","nome":"Russian","termine":"тарака́н","categoria":"non_precisato"}],"lontana":"ru","ambiti":[],"via":"","testo":"תִּיק (tík, “bag”) + ־ָן (-án), due to the egg sack a cockroach carries. Perhaps inspired phonetically by Russian тарака́н (tarakán)."}]}